WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:02.260
Narrator: Imagine having so many children,

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:04.460
you could run a factory.

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:07.560
That's what Moulay Ismail's
family looked like.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:11.250
He was a brutal emperor of
the Moroccan Alaouite Dynasty

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:14.870
from 1672 to 1727,

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:17.962
and he was reported to have had at least

00:00:17.962 --> 00:00:22.178
1,171 children.

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:23.520
But he wasn't the only one

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:26.640
who used his power to sleep
with hundreds of women,

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.410
whether they were interested or not.

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:31.610
Other rulers like Augustus the Strong,

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:34.509
and Genghis Khan had hundreds of children,

00:00:34.509 --> 00:00:37.810
and while these were some
of the more ruthless rulers

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:39.260
of their time,

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:42.743
it raises a more fundamental
scientific question.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:47.800
Women can reproduce for
about half their lifetime

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:51.410
and can only give birth
about once every year or so,

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:53.820
so it makes sense that women
can only have a fraction

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:56.010
as many children as men.

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:57.070
One study estimated

00:00:57.070 --> 00:00:59.590
that women can have around 15 pregnancies

00:00:59.590 --> 00:01:02.530
in a lifetime, and
depending on how many babies

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:04.820
she gives birth to at a time,

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:08.990
a woman can probably have
around 15 to 30 children max.

00:01:08.990 --> 00:01:10.980
But the most prolific mother ever,

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:12.550
according to Guinness World Records,

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:16.580
was Mrs. Feodor Vassilyev
in 19th-century Russia.

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:19.230
She is said to have given
birth to 69 children

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:21.350
over 27 pregnancies.

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:23.070
That's a lot for one woman,

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:24.760
but that's nothing compared to our friend

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:27.030
from earlier, Moulay Ismail.

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:28.710
According to records, he had four wives

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:31.410
and 500 women in his harem,

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:33.760
but there are factors
that not even an emperor

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:37.580
can control, like how a man's
sperm becomes less mobile

00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:40.640
and more abnormal as he grows older,

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:43.070
which ultimately reduces his chances

00:01:43.070 --> 00:01:45.810
of fathering children later in life.

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:49.180
In fact, studies suggest that men over 50

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:51.900
have an up to 38% lower chance

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:53.250
of impregnating a woman

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:55.790
compared to men under 30.

00:01:55.790 --> 00:01:57.420
For Ismail, he fathered most

00:01:57.420 --> 00:01:59.820
of his children relatively young,

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:02.232
so by age 57, he had an estimated 

00:02:02.232 --> 00:02:06.594
1,171 kids.

00:02:06.594 --> 00:02:08.440
But he wasn't the only man in history

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:10.320
with tons of progeny.

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:13.820
Augustus the Strong was
king of 18th-century Poland,

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:18.140
and he had a long distance
relationship with his wife.

00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:20.030
So, of course that didn't stop him

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:25.000
from fathering a rumored
370 children by mistresses,

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:28.490
and Genghis Khan, notorious
for conquering large areas

00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:30.190
of 13th-century Asia

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:35.190
is estimated to have had between
1,000 and 2,000 children.

00:02:35.290 --> 00:02:38.663
In fact, by tracking
types of Y chromosomes,

00:02:38.663 --> 00:02:43.060
scientists estimate that
up to 16 million men today,

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:45.600
who live in regions that Khan conquered,

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.520
could have been descendants of him

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:49.800
or his close male relatives.

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:51.640
But did these men really reach

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:54.190
their maximum human possibility?

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:55.940
Turns out the records on Ismail

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:59.000
only spanned 32 years of his life.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:02.670
By one calculation, he really
could have had hundreds more.

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:05.340
If you compare that to
men in more modern times,

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:08.180
the most prolific fathers today

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:11.120
have about 200 children.

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:15.030
That's nowhere near 1,171,

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:17.373
and honestly, it's probably for the best.

